<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Experimental Settings</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To facilitate reproducibility and provide a clear overview of our extensive experimental evaluation (<math id="A4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q1</annotation></semantics></math> through <math id="A4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q15</annotation></semantics></math>), we summarize the master configuration for all experiments in this section. Table <a href="#A4.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ Appendix D Experimental Settings ‣ Understanding LoRA as Knowledge Memory: An Empirical Analysis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> maps each research question to its specific experimental setup, including the dataset, base model, and key variable parameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T3" class="ltx_table">
